  {
    "source": {
      "type": "ical",
      "iCalUid": "353999@www.d125.org"
    },
    "title": "CCC - Senior Family Night",
    "categories": [
      "CCC"
    ],
    "timing": {
      "allDay": false,
      "start": "2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z",
      "end": "2026-08-25T00:00:00.000Z"
    },
    "location": "West Auditorium",
    "description": "The College Career Center will hold its annual Senior Family Night from 7-8:30 p.m. on Monday, Aug. 24. The event will be in the West Auditorium (located by the Point Entrance) and  live-streamed through Zoom . It is open to all parents and guardians of seniors at Stevenson.\n \n\n During the presentation, Post Secondary Counselor Sara Hanson and Dan Miller will discuss how to apply to colleges. Topics to be covered include types of applications (Common App, for example), admission plans (including Early Decision), deadlines, obtaining a transcript, standardized test scores, letters of recommendation, essays and scholarships.\n \n\n The slides and the recording will be accessible on our website within a week of the event."
  },
